cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this candidate, its ephemeris or this code, please cite it as below."
title: "TIC 240488148.01: a 1.4 Earth-radius, 1.51-day transiting planet candidate around the nearby K dwarf TIC 240488148"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Paliwal
    given-names: Advait
    email: advaitpaliwal@gmail.com
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/advaitpaliwal/TIC240488148"
url: "https://github.com/advaitpaliwal/TIC240488148"
abstract: >-
  A transit-like signal on TIC 240488148 (TYC 3191-503-1), a K dwarf at 58.7 pc,
  found on 2026-10-08 in TESS full-frame-image photometry from Sectors 15, 16, 56,
  76, 82 and 83. Period 1.5125149 +/- 0.0000029 d, mid-transit BJD_TDB
  2460393.34348 +/- 0.0013, depth 411 +/- 28 ppm, duration 1.41 h, radius
  1.37 +/- 0.14 Earth radii. False-positive probability 0.024 with Gaia companion
  limits, so a planet candidate, not a validated planet.
keywords:
  - exoplanet
  - transit
  - TESS
  - planet candidate
  - TIC 240488148
